{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1513807-they-put-a-freehold-on-the-moon","id":1513807,"title":"They put a Freehold ON THE MOON!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-06-03T13:02:48-07:00","id":1513807,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon6.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> They put a Freehold ON THE MOON!","content":"So, Kith and Kin introduces the concept of Changelings... IN SPACE! and even gives an extremely brief write up about a Freehold on the Moon. Unfortunately what is given is not actually all that detailed and I don't particularly like it that much (sorry to whoever wrote it, you did a great job sparking my imagination though). I really want to expand upon that, possibly for Storyteller's Vault. So I'm creating a new setting. I call it Selene.<br /> Selene is <i>extremely</i> different from the Changeling we're familiar with, and comes straight to you out of a Frank Franzetta painting of a Princess of Mars cover. This is a place where you might do battle with Mi-Go or shapeshifting spirits. It's a setting where the second star to the right and straight on til morning will lead to a world of adventure.<br /> <br /> It departs heavily from the Lunar Freehold given in the book. First, the Court System is completely different. There are five courts, each dedicated to one of the Celestial Maidens that the earliest freehold bargained with. Second, there are humans on the moon. These two facts are related. The foundational myth of Selene, though the actual details are lost to the generations, is that the earliest Changelings on the moon for hundreds of years were simply Free Companies. Stories abound going back thousands of years of people living on the moon, and these Changelings might have inspired those stories, or the Gentry that created them might have <i>been</i> inspired by them. Either way, they came out in a lifeless world but somehow managed to stay. Meanwhile, the other major group were the people of Habitat 3D3N. They were not taken by the Gentry, but their ancestors were taken by Angels. Those ancestors lived on the far side of the moon in paradise, but that time was long since passed as the Infrastructure that kept Habitat 3D3N running was failing.<br /> This is when the Five Maidens came to the Free Companies of the Moon, which conveniently numbered Five. They were Mercury, Venus, Mars, Jupiter, and Saturn (sometimes known as the Crone). Each offered the Free Companies power and protection\u2014the Moon is a Harsh Mistress after all\u2014if they chose to aid the people flee Eden (and worshiped the Maidens). And so the Free Companies earned their Bargains. The Court of Journeys lead the way, seeking out the best paths. The Court of Serenity tended to the Integrity of the refugees and fed them as they traveled. The Court of Battles protected them from the myriad threats found crossing Oceanus Procellarum. The Court of Secrets hid them away from the most dangerous things. And the Court of Endings watched over it all and guided the change. Bargains in hand, the arduous trek through complete, the Freehold of Selene was well and truly established.<br /> <br /> That was maybe a hundred years ago. Since then, the people of Selene have built a city on the Moon. Though I'm leaving the specifics up to anyone who uses the setting (I think somewhere in Oceanus Procellarum or Mare Tranquillitatis is thematically appropriate). Selene holds many secrets, as the Jovians will tell you. Civilizations the God Machine abandoned that were forced to fend for themselves and fell centuries ago. Fallen Lychgates, crafted by the Huntsmen before the Gentry came to Arcadia. And of course simply swashbuckling space faring adventure as you fight off the migou.<br /> <br /> <b>Mercury \u2014 Journeys</b><br /> Mercurian; Explorers, Wanderers<br /> The Court of Mercury are explorers. They may have their homes, but they also want to venture among the stars. Many of them didn\u2019t originate on Selene, they came to her from Earth on the Wishing Roads because they felt the call of the Maiden of Journeys. They\u2019re also the ones who want to expand Selene\u2019s reaches well beyond the Kuiper Belt, and are the reason that there are some tiny little places on Io and Mars.<br /> The Maiden herself watches over the Wishing Roads, and her courtiers explore them with abandon, though her protection isn\u2019t perfect. But then again, the Explorers wouldn\u2019t want it any other way.<br /> Emotion: Wonder<br /> <br /> <b>Venus \u2014 Serenity</b><br /> Venusian; (Moon) Rabbits, Gardeners<br /> The Court of Serenity are empathetic and caring, and keep the Freehold of Selene running. They create flourishing hedge gardens that are welcome to all, and make sure to try helping the other Courtiers with their problems. They are the volunteers without whom Selene would simply be a dead rock floating in space.<br /> The Maiden herself makes Selene able to grow food, both fae and mortal. Her bounty is tended to by her acolytes.<br /> Emotion: Compassion<br /> <br /> <b>Mars \u2014 Battle</b><br /> Martian; Warriors, Tacticians<br /> The Moon is a harsh mistress. While the other Celestial Courts might try to tame it, the Chosen of Battles makes sure that it stays in one piece. The Gentry aren\u2019t the only threat the Court of Battle has to face. Strange shapeshifting horrors lurk in the dark, and even stranger alien threats abound. The Martian Courtiers fight those threats as well, clashing against them with spear and sword and magic.<br /> The Bargain with the Maiden of Battle protects Selene from the Idigam, Angels of the God-Machine, and greater threats that would obliterate Selene. The formless spirit monsters, Huntsmen, and fungal aliens that slip through, her children take care of.<br /> Emotion: Tenacity<br /> <br /> <b>Jupiter \u2014 Secrets</b><br /> Jovian; Tattletales, Treasure Keepers<br /> The Jovian Court hunts down secrets. Not simply to hoard the arcane and dangerous knowledge away\u2014though they do that as well\u2014but also to reveal the secrets, even when doing so causes trouble. They are forever driven by the desire to know what\u2019s in the box, as well as the joy in hiding something in a box from others.<br /> The Maiden of Secrets protects Selene by covering the Freehold from the prying eyes of both Supernatural and Terrestrial agents. The blanket of secrecy isn\u2019t perfect, though, and her chosen keep the Freehold from leaving traces.<br /> Emotion: Curiosity<br /> <br /> <b>Saturn \u2014 Endings</b><br /> Saturnine; Judges, Crones<br /> The Maiden Saturn, sometimes called the Crone, is the final arbiter of all. She and her Court oversee the end of all things and the crushing void of space. But as with the Tarot Death, she isn\u2019t simply a complete ending, but instead change. One door opens and another closes. They are the opportunity of the void. They act as judges of the Freehold, meting out punishments and calling for restitution.<br /> The Crone grants her blessing to Selene by allowing the Freehold to breathe, the void of her star ocean parting for the area around the Freehold.<br /> Emotion: Resignation<br /> \u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":2998,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","user":"Aspel","date":".  What are you, a cop? 06-03-2023, 04:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-04T03:09:17-07:00","id":1513853,"title":"","content":"I have created Mantles.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial Mantle</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Chosen of Journeys join the Court because they want to see beyond the horizon, not simply geographically (or astrologically, as the case often is) but spiritually. They gain a point of Glamour whenever intentionally getting lost in something new. This could be a place, or it could be a hobby, or social group. That sense of confusion and excitement at the novel is key.<br /> The Mantle tinges a changeling\u2019s mien with glittering stars and a sense of awe. Many manifest a pole star above their brow.<br /> \u25cf Gain a bonus equal to your mantle to mundane Athletics rolls for travel.<br /> \u25cf\u25cf Gain bonus dice equal to your mantle on rolls to guide others.<br /> \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf Reduce the target number for chases by 2 successes.<br /> \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf Reduce the cost of contracts used to travel by 1 glamour.<br /> \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf By touching someone and spending a point of glamour, you can comprehend any language they know for the scene, and speak it if capable.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Venusian Mantle</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Chosen of Serenity are level headed and caring, and willing to put in the effort to help others. They regain a point of glamour whenever they dedicate a significant amount of time to tend to someone else\u2019s material needs.<br /> The Mantle manifests as the calming voice of a distant song and Selenian petrichor. At higher ratings, they have the dusty impression of rabbit ears around their head.<br /> \u25cf Gain a bonus equal to your mantle on mundane rolls to cultivate something that benefits others.<br /> \u25cf\u25cf Gain a bonus equal to your mantle on mundane rolls to prepare for a celebration or event.<br /> \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf Another character may, once per chapter, choose to treat you as a Touchstone for the purposes of healing Clarity.<br /> \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf So long as you haven\u2019t done harm, if someone deals damaged to you, they become Beaten Down and it costs 2 points of Willpower to shake off.<br /> \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf Once per chapter you may spend a point of willpower to grant the Inspired condition to up to five people.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Martian Mantle</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Chosen of Battles are warriors of a special kind, they\u2019re warriors of the mind. They know how to strike and where and when to undermine their enemy\u2019s defenses and bring a conflict to a swift end, ideally without death. They gain a point of glamour when engaging in combat that they\u2019re prepared for.<br /> The Martian Mantle manifests as the smell of sweat and even blood, and the hands of the children of Mars often become burnished bronze.<br /> \u25cf Reduce the Initiative penalty of any equipment you\u2019ve trained with by your mantle rating.<br /> \u25cf\u25cf Reduce the penalty of a Build Equipment action to create a plan designed to engage in, prevent, or defend against violence by your mantle rating. This doesn\u2019t decrease the time, and doesn\u2019t include Jury Rigging.<br /> \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf As long as you\u2019re close enough to someone to protect them, you grant half your mantle rating in Defense bonus (rounded up).<br /> \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf Any time someone fills one of an ally\u2019s last three health boxes with lethal damage, you may spend a point of glamour to lash out with a strike that deals damage equal to your Mantle.<br /> \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf Once per chapter you can reflexively Dodge an attack, even if you\u2019ve already acted in the turn or choose to act later. You deal damage equal to the excess successes (don\u2019t add your weapon damage) <b>or</b> can initiate a grapple.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jovian Mantle</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Chosen of Secrets are constantly obsessing about anything that might be hidden, never deterred by any danger they might face for doing so. They aren\u2019t usually malicious in this, they just want to know everything there is. It\u2019s the finding and keeping of secrets that\u2019s the real draw. They gain a point of glamour when they finally discover a difficult secret or solve a challenging puzzle.<br /> The mantle of Secrets makes it\u2019s children harder to spot, at least until they want to be seen. The Tattletales will often be translucent unless you\u2019re looking right at them, and when their curiosity is piqued they give off the smell of ozone and the crackle of excited thunder.<br /> \u25cf You gain a bonus equal to your mantle dots on any mundane rolls to solve puzzles or uncover someone\u2019s secrets.<br /> \u25cf\u25cf Whenever spend an element from a Clue, the bonus it grants is equal to your Mantle rating.<br /> \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf Whenever you stalk someone, their attempts to spot you are penalized by your mantle.<br /> \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf The secrets you keep stay hidden. Spend 1 point of glamour to hide something up to size 3 in plain sight. Finding it requires actively looking and takes a penalty equal to your mantle. People will move papers without noticing it, and simply sidestep a safe without thinking.<br /> \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf Once per chapter when you reveal someone\u2019s hidden secrets they gain a Condition of your choice from Broken, Guilty, or Notoriety.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saturnine Mantle</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Mantle of Endings gives the Chosen an air of finality. Their hands, and at higher levels their eyes, take on the appearance of the void, complete with starlight that reveals constellations not of this world. A paraselene forms around their head, complete with moon dogs.<br /> Crones gain a point of glamour when dispatching a dangerous threat through esoteric means.<br /> \u25cf You gain bonus dice equal to your mantle rating to understand and judge disputes.<br /> \u25cf\u25cf Any attempt to deduce what you\u2019re thinking or understand your motives suffers a penalty to your mantle rating unless the opposition spends a point of willpower that doesn\u2019t grant a bonus.<br /> \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf You gain a bonus equal to your mantle rating to mundane rolls to interact with esoteric entities [editor's note: ephemeral entities and Horrors like the migou], and may seal pledges with them.<br /> \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf You may ignore the passage of time, removing yourself from Initiative and acting for one turn without interference (so long as you don\u2019t interfere with anyone else). The Crone takes her price in Goblin Debt.<br /> \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf Once per chapter you may perform a ritual (creating mystical equipment) to designate yourself the minor Bane of an esoteric supernatural entity. The roll suffers a penalty equal to the entity in question\u2019s Rank or Potency, and may require special equipment of it\u2019s own. When complete the entity must spend a Willpower point any time it wants to act against you and the first time it does so it takes lethal damage equal to your Mantle rating.</div> </div> </div> </div>I kinda feel like they got more complex and interesting as I went along, leaving Chosen of Journeys sort of... getting the job done, but not being fancy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":2998,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","user":"Aspel","date":". 06-04-2023, 06:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}